          "title": "4. Combination reactions",
          "text": "In a combination reaction, two or more reactants combine to form a single product. The general pattern is A + B → AB. Calcium oxide reacts with water to give calcium hydroxide: CaO(s) + H₂O(l) → Ca(OH)₂(aq). Burning carbon in oxygen gives carbon dioxide: C(s) + O₂(g) → CO₂(g). The defining structural feature is one product, not the amount of heat released."
